   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">This will successfully generate an the same plot:<div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ggvis</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>mtcars </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ggvis</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cyl</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> layer_histograms</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>mtcars </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ggvis</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> layer_histograms</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cyl</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div>This too is successful:</div><div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">vis </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mtcars </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ggvis</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>vis </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> layer_histograms</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cyl</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>But this is not:</div><div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">vis </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mtcars </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ggvis</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>vis_verb </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">layer_histograms</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cyl</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#800\">## This fails with &#39;</span><font color=\"#ff0000\"><span style=\"color:#800\">Error: Can&#39;t find prop x.update</span></font><span style=\"color:#800\">&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>vis </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> vis_verb</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div>nor is this:</div><div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">vis </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mtcars </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ggvis</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>vis_verb </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\">layer_histograms</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cyl</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>vis </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> vis_verb </span><span style=\"color:#800\">## This fails w &#39;Error in vis_verb(.) : unused argument (.)&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div>Why do the latter two examples fail?  What am I missing?</div><div><br></div><div>Maybe this is more of a basic R question-- I would welcome being pointed in the right direction.  Thank you for any insight.<br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "kmNiRLiuCx0J",
   "from": "Ista Zahn",
   "author": "373beb702917b8b5",
   "date": "2015-05-12T02:16:08Z",
   "subject": "Re: Fundamental ggvis behavior",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<p dir=\"ltr\">The short answer is that the first argument to the layer_* functions<br>\r\nis always a vis object (as created by ggvis). You&#39;re failing examples<br>\r\ndon&#39;t give layer_histogram a vis so it doesn&#39;t know what to do. It&#39;s<br>\r\nadmittedly hard to see that because of the piping; things become<br>\r\nclearer I think if you avoid it:</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">## these all work (notice that the first argument<br>\r\n## to layer_histograms is always a ggvis object):<br>\r\nlayer_histograms(ggvis(mtcars, ~cyl))<br>\r\nlayer_histograms(ggvis(mtcars), ~cyl)<br>\r\nvis &lt;- ggvis(mtcars)<br>\r\nlayer_histograms(vis, ~cyl)</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">## this doesn&#39;t work, because the first argument<br>\r\n## to layer_histogram is not a vis object produced<br>\r\n## by ggvis:<br>\r\nvis_verb &lt;-layer_histograms(~cyl)</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Hope this helps,<br>\r\nIsta</p>\r\n<div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\">On May 11, 2015 7:01 PM, &quot;ArjunaCap&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mcaw...@greenstenergy.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br type=\"attribution\"></div>"
    ],
    [
